<!-- A member of a local cluster behind a front node (conf/front/README.md; plans/Edge-Node2.md §4.7): every member runs
    this conf, on one external database, and links to the front node on its own with the pairing's key. The front node
    (node_role front, conf/front/MoquiFrontConf.xml) pools the members linked for the pairing and balances its host
    names over the live ones, behind its web protection, so no load balancer of your own is needed, and the members need
    no open port, port forward or fixed address. It is conf/local-cluster/MoquiPooledConf.xml with a front node in the
    edge node's place: that conf's comments on the database, the secrets, admission and draining hold here as they are,
    and this one says what differs. A front has none of the edge set, so the cluster keeps its own mail, chat, calls,
    phones and PASS, or has none. Use the Enterprise package (--enterprise), as for any cluster. -->
<moqui-conf xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://moqui.org/xsd/moqui-conf-3.xsd">
    <default-property name="instance_purpose" value="production"/>

    <!-- The shared database, as in conf/local-cluster: Postgres (or MySQL with the default cluster transport), its
        settings in .env, the same on every member. Back it up with its own tools: the backup job covers an embedded
        database only. -->
    <default-property name="entity_ds_db_conf" value="postgres"/>

    <!-- The same .env on every member: the secrets the first member's first start generates (session_cookie_key,
        cluster_tls_cert, cluster_tls_key, entity_ds_crypt_pass) and what pairing with the front writes on that member:
        front_node_url, front_node_key (the pairing's key), front_node_pin and front_node_id. A front pairing has no
        pairing id: the front knows the cluster by its key and its members' ids, and there is no queue. Copy that whole
        .env to every other member, then add the member's own cluster_base_url, https://(this member's private
        address):8444; each links at its next start. Each member's own: its instance id (runtime/db/instance_id), its
        member key (runtime/db/edge_member_key) and the front's member list (runtime/db/front_members). Never copy
        runtime/db between members. Open 8444 between the members only.
        Admission is as with an edge node: while a member is linked, a new one is admitted only when a linked member's
        cluster lists it as live, so a copy on another database with the key is refused "join the cluster first". -->
    <default-property name="cluster_transport" value=""/>
    <default-property name="cluster_protocol" value=""/>

    <!-- Web access through the front: the client's address comes over the link, so no webapp_trusted_proxies or
        webapp_client_ip_header; each member's web protection counts by it, and a ban one member starts is shared with
        the others and told up the link, so the front refuses that client for this pairing's names. The wizard
        (System › Edge Node, Set up again) sends the host names, each in its mode: a passthrough name ends its TLS on
        the member, so each member needs its certificate in runtime/cert (the same files on each); a terminate name ends
        on the front, which needs its certificate, and is balanced sticky by the session cookie. Sessions are rows in
        the shared database, so the session-config flush="guarantee" of conf/local-cluster/MoquiLocalConf.xml is not
        needed: a member writes a new session before its response, as one pooled by an edge node does. -->

    <!-- What stays the cluster's own, since the front has none of the edge set:
        mail out: an EmailServer with an outside relay or the provider's SMTP, as on one server;
        mail in: an IMAP sync, or the SMTP listener on every member in internet mode (smtp_listen_port, smtp_internet=true,
            smtp_hostname; docs/interfaces/Mail-Inbound.md) with port 25 on the front as an EdgePort row of kind smtp
            for this pairing, which passes each connection to a live member with a PROXY header naming the client (the
            code takes it as for an edge cluster's members, but this path to a local cluster has no test yet);
        chat bridges and SMS: channels_webhooks_enabled=true and channels_public_url, one of the cluster's host names
            through the front (a terminate name);
        calls: the members' own media nodes and TURN, at addresses of their own, never through the front
            (docs/interfaces/WebRTC.md, Cluster);
        phones: SIP at the members' own addresses, never through the front;
        XMPP: the front's XMPP ports take this node's xmpp_domain when the wizard sends it;
        PASS: PASS servers of your own reach the cluster as their authority over its host names (conf/pass). -->

    <!-- Draining and rolling upgrades, as in conf/local-cluster/MoquiPooledConf.xml: drain a member on its own System ›
        Edge Node (This node's cluster) or on the front's Edge Clients › Clients; the front sends it no new work and its
        /health answers 503. Draining the only live member takes the pairing's names offline at the front. -->

    <entity-facade crypt-pass="${entity_ds_crypt_pass}" query-stats="true"/>
</moqui-conf>
